          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Künneth theorem
            is a statement relating the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of two objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            with that of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
          %p
            In good situations it identifies the (co)homology of a product with the tensor product of the (co)homologies:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(X \times Y, E) \simeq H^\bullet(X,E) \otimes H^\bullet(Y,E)
            = succeed "-groups." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
          %h2#statement Statement
          %h3#InOrdinaryHomology In ordinary homology
          %p
            We discuss the Künneth theorem in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo =
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} = R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} Mod \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            is the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_1, N_2 \in R Mod
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_1 \otimes N_2 \in R Mod
            for their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mo •
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet, C'_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
            two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            of
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C \otimes_R C')_\bullet
            for their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Tor
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tor^R_1(N_1,N_2)
            for the first
            = succeed "-module" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_1
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_2
          %p
            We discuss the Künneth theorem over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            in stages, starting with important special cases and then passing to more general statements.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InOrdinaryHomologyOverAField"} Over a field
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OverAPrincipalIdealDomain"} Over a principal ideal domain
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OverGeneralRings"} Over a general ring
          %p
            All these versions hold for chain homology and tensor products of general chain complexes. But under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+theorem"} Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
            all these statements apply directly in particular to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and their products. This is discussed below in
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#InOrdinaryHomologyForTopologicalSpaces"} For singular homology of products of topological spaces
          %h4#InOrdinaryHomologyOverAField Over a field
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
          #InordinaryHomologyOverAField.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mo •
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet,C'_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(k Vect)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi m
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi m
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi m
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo •
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mo •
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\oplus_m \left(
                    H_m\left(C_\bullet\right) \otimes_k H_{n-m}\left(C'_\bullet\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    H_n\left(
                    C_\bullet \otimes_k C'_\bullet
                    \\right)
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              of chain homologies.
          %p
            For a proof see the proof of theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InordinaryHomology"}
            below, of which this is a special case.
          %h4#OverAPrincipalIdealDomain Over a principal ideal domain
          %p
            Let now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ideal+domain"} principal ideal domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            as above, or for instance it may be the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          #InordinaryHomology.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ideal+domain"} principal ideal domain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+modules"} free modules
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              and given any other chain complex
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mo •
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo •
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mo •
                      %mo )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Tor
                      %mn 1
                      %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\to
                    \\oplus_k \left(
                    H_k\left(C_\bullet\right) \otimes_R H_{n-k}\left(C'_\bullet\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\to
                    H_n\left(
                    C_\bullet \otimes_R C'_\bullet
                    \\right)
                    \\to
                    \\oplus_k
                    Tor_1^R\left(H_k\left(C_\bullet\right), H_{n-k-1}\left(C'_\bullet\right)\right)
                    \\to
                    0
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, theorem 3B.5
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In the special case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              is concentrated in degree 0, this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
              in ordinary homology.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              In particular if all the
              = succeed "-groups" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mo •
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo •
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mo •
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\oplus_k \left(
                    H_k\left(C_\bullet\right) \otimes_R H_{n-k}\left(C'_\bullet\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    H_n\left(
                    C_\bullet \otimes_R C'_\bullet
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is the case (assuming the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              (since every module over a field is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              – every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+of+a+free+module"} basis
              – and every free module is a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat module
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              %strong
                of theorem
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InordinaryHomology"}
            %p
              Notice that since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_k
              is assumed to be free, hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              with itself, since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
              distributes over direct sums, and since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              respects direct sums, we have
            #eq:A.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(C_k \otimes_R C')
                    \\simeq
                    C_k \otimes_R H_{n-k}(C'_\bullet)
                    \\,.
            %p
              First consider now the special case that all the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_k(C_\bullet) = C_k
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:A"} (1)
              yields
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(C_k \otimes_R C') \simeq H_k(C_\bullet) \otimes_R H_{n-k}(C'_\bullet)
              and therefore
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi R
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊕
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi R
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊕
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi R
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊕
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi R
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mo ′
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    H_n(C \otimes_R C')
                    \&amp;\simeq
                    H_n(\oplus_k C_k \otimes_R C' ))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\oplus_k H_n( C_k \otimes_R C' )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\oplus_k H_k(C_\bullet) \otimes_R H_{n-k}(C'_\bullet)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_k(C) = C_k
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              by assumption, it has no
              = succeed "-terms" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
            %p
              Now let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet
              be a general chain complex of free modules. Notice that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi k
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to Z_{n-k} \hookrightarrow C_{n-k} \stackrel{\partial_{n-k-1}}{\to} B_{n-1} \to 0
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequence"} splits
              due to the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequence"} split exact sequence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              decomposition
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Z
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n \simeq Z_n \oplus B_{n-1}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
              distributes over direct sum, it follows that tensoring with any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'_k
              yields another
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\to
                    Z_{n-k} \otimes_R C'_k
                    \\to
                    C_{n-k} \otimes_R C'_k
                    \\to
                    B_{n-k-1} \otimes_R C'_k
                    \\to
                    0
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that if we regard the graded modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z_\bullet
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_\bullet
              of chains and of boundaries as chain complexes with zero-differentials, then we have a short exact sequence of chain complexes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to Z_\bullet \otimes_R C'_\bullet \to C_\bullet \otimes_R C'_\bullet \to B_{\bullet-1}\otimes_R C'_\bullet  \to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              This induces its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+long+exact+sequence"} homology long exact sequence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    H_n( Z \otimes_R C')
                    \\to
                    H_n( C \times_R C' )
                    \\to
                    H_{n-1}( B \otimes_R C' )
                    \\to
                    H_{n-1}( Z \otimes_R C' )
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here the terms involving the complexes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              of boundaries and cycles may be evalutated, since these have zero differentials, via the special case discussed at the beginning of this proof to yield the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi R
                        %mi C
                        %mo ′
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\stackrel{i_n \otimes_R C'}{\to}
                    \\oplus_k ( Z_k \otimes_R H_{n-k}(C') )
                    \\to
                    H_n(C \otimes_R C')
                    \\to
                    \\oplus_{k}( B_k \otimes_R H_{n-k-1}(C') )
                    \\stackrel{i_{n-1}}{\to}
                    \\oplus_k ( Z_k \otimes_R H_{n-k-1}(C') )
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_n \coloneqq H_n(i \otimes C')
              is the morphism induced from the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mo •
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon B_\bullet \hookrightarrow Z_\bullet
              of boundaries into cycles.
            %p
              This means that by quotienting out an image on the left and a kernel on the right, we obtain a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\to
                    coker(i_n)
                    \\to
                    H_n(C \otimes_R C')
                    \\to
                    ker(i_{n-1})
                    \\to
                    0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+exact+functor"} right exact functor
              it commutes with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              on the left, as does the formation of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coker
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi k
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mi k
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi C
                              %mo ′
                              %mo )
                        %msub
                          %mi Z
                          %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi C
                          %mo ′
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi coker
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi B
                            %mi k
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mi Z
                            %mi k
                          %mo )
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi C
                        %mo )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ′
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    coker\left( \oplus_k \left(
                    B_k \otimes_R H_{n-k}(C')
                    \\stackrel{i_k \otimes H_{n-k}\left(C'\right)}{\to}
                    Z_k \otimes_R H_{n-k}\left(C'\right)
                    \\right)\right)
                    \\simeq
                    \\oplus_k \left(
                    \\left(
                    coker\left(B_k \stackrel{i_k}{\to} Z_k\right)
                    \\otimes_R
                    H_{n-k}(C')
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\simeq
                    \\oplus_k
                    \\left(
                    H_k\left(C\right) \otimes_R H_{n-k}\left(C'\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is the left term in the short exact sequence to be shown. For the right term the analogous argument does not quite go through, because tensoring is not in addition a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact functor
              = succeed "-module:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
            %p
              Notice that by the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
              is free and using the fact (discussed at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ideal+domain"} principal ideal domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              the submodules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_n, Z_n \hookrightarrow C_n
              are themselves free modules, the defining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to B_n \stackrel{i_n}{\to} Z_n \to H_n(C) \to 0
              exhibits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolution"} projective resolution
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(C)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Tor
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ker
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi k
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Tor_1(H_k(C), H_{n-k}(C'))
                    \\simeq
                    ker\left(
                    i_k \otimes H_{n-k}(C')
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p This identifies the term on the right of the exact sequence to be shown.
          %h4#OverGeneralRings Over general rings
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            any ring, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
            converging to the homology of the tensor product, whose second page involves all the
            = succeed "-modules:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%BCnneth+spectral+sequence"} Künneth spectral sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi q
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Tor
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_{p,q}^2
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\oplus_{k_1 + k_2 = q}
                  Tor_p^{R Mod}( H_{k_1}(C), H_{k_2}(C'))
                  \\Rightarrow
                  H_{p+q}(C \otimes C')
          %p (…)
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Williams"}> Williams, section 4.2
            ).
          %h3#InOrdinaryCohomology In ordinary cohomology
          #KunnethInOrdinaryCohomology.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^k(Y,R)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^\bullet(X,R)
                    \\otimes_R
                    H^\bullet(Y,R)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    H^\bullet(X\times Y, R)
            %p
              (from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+rings"} cohomology rings
              to the cohomology ring of the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Hatcher"} Hatcher (2001), theorem 3.15
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Spanier77"} Spanier (1966), section 5.5, theorem 11
            %a{:href => "#Weibel94"} Weibel (1994), Thm. 3.6.1
          %h3#in_generalised_cohomology_theories In Generalised cohomology theories
          %p
            The Künneth theorem for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalised+cohomology+theories"} generalised cohomology theories
            is a special case of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            two
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            as the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} module spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \coloneqq F(Y, E)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(-,-)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+spectrum"} function spectrum
            (that is, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            in the category of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology"} reduced
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in this cohomology theory is thus given by:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G^*(X) = [X,F(Y,E)] = [X \wedge Y,E] = E^*(X \wedge Y)
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
            gives a way of computing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^*(X)
            from knowledge of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*(X)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi pt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^*(pt)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi pt
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^*(pt) = E^*(Y)
            so our initial data is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*(X)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*(Y)
          %p
            For more details, see the page on the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#InOrdinaryHomologyForTopologicalSpaces For singular homology of products of topological spaces
          %p
            All of these statements have their analogs for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X , Y \in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+theorem"} Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi qi
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_\bullet(X \times Y)
                  \\simeq_{qi}
                  C_\bullet(X) \otimes C_\bullet(Y)
          %p
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+chain+complex"} singular chain complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product space
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            of the separate singular chain complexes. Hence in particular there are isomorphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_n(X \times Y) \simeq
                  H_n(C_\bullet(X) \otimes C_\bullet(Y))
                  \\,.
          %p Using this in the above statements of the Künneth theorem yields directly the Künneth theorem for singular homology of topological spaces.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+theorem"} Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
          %h2#references References
          %h3#in_ordinary_cohomology_2 In ordinary (co)homology
          %p The original articles are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                H. Künneth,
                %em Über die Bettischen Zahlen einer Produktmannigfaltigkeit
                Math. Ann. , 90 (1923) pp. 65–85
            %li
              %p
                H. Künneth,
                %em Über die Torsionszahlen von Produktmannigfaltigkeiten
                Math. Ann. , 91 (1924) pp. 125–134
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Spanier66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Spanier"}> Edwin Spanier
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4684-9322-1"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4684-9322-1
            %li#Hatcher
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
                , Section
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATch3.4.pdf"} 3.B
                of:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATpage.html"} Algebraic topology
                (2001)
            %li#Weibel94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Weibel"}> Charles Weibel
                , Section 3.6 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/An+introduction+to+homological+algebra"} An introduction to homological algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 38
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139644136"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139644136
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug//otherpapers/weibel-hom.pdf"} pdf
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Rob Thompson,
                %em Products and the Künneth theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.hunter.cuny.edu/~rthompso/topology_notes/chapter%20nine.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Williams
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brandon+Williams"}> Brandon Williams
                , Section 4.2 in
                %em Spectral sequences
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.sunysb.edu/~mbw/notes/orals/Spectral%20Sequences.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
                , section 22 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+%C3%89tale+Cohomology"} Lectures on Étale Cohomology
          %h3#in_generalized_cohomology In generalized (co)homology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              , part II, section 6.2 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
              (2012)
          %p
            See also the corresponding references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectra"} parameterized spectra
          %ul
            %li#MaySigurdsson06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              , J. Sigurdsson, section 22.7 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Parametrized+Homotopy+Theory"} Parametrized Homotopy Theory
